        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cd158dda-c53a-5c91-a50b-8517c0de53c8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Courtney Love, Arabella Field, Steven Baigelman, Keanu Reeves, Vincent D'Onofrio, Cameron Diaz, Tuesday Weld, Dan Aykroyd, Delroy Lindo, Dave Callahan, Paul Clark, Andy Golding, Andy Bolton, Frank Stebbing\n- Bands: Hole, The Wolfhounds\n- Films: Feeling Minnesota\n- Places: Romford, UK\n\nFacts:\n- Courtney Love was born as Courtney Michelle Harrison on July 9, 1964, and she is an American singer, songwriter, actress, and visual artist.\n- Arabella Field was born on February 5, 1965, and she is an American actress and film producer.\n- The Wolfhounds were formed in Romford, UK in 1985 by Dave Callahan, Paul Clark, Andy Golding, Andy Bolton, and Frank Stebbing, and the band was originally active until 1990.\n- Courtney Love formed the alternative rock band Hole in 1989 and rose to prominence as its frontwoman.\n- Feeling Minnesota is a 1996 American crime drama comedy film written and directed by Steven Baigelman.\n- Feeling Minnesota stars Keanu Reeves, Vincent D'Onofrio, Cameron Diaz, Tuesday Weld, Dan Aykroyd, Delroy Lindo, and Courtney Love.\n- Arabella Field is known for roles in the films Dante's Peak, Feeling Minnesota, Godzilla, National Treasure, and Paper Man, and for voicing Melinda Bitterman in the animated television version of Baby Blues.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
